    "product_id": "88964e6e-8519-4e36-8fb0-e67de435b4f5",
    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 021147\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n445 AM PDT Wed Sep 2 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n*  Drier, cooler, and breezy conditions expected through the work \n   week.  \n\n*  Uncertainty increases this weekend with regards to tropical\n   moisture from Marie. \n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...Wednesday through Monday.\n\nDrier air will eliminate precipitation chances through Friday for \nmost locations as a trough deepens over the west coast and PWATs \nfall to half an inch or less. A few isolated storms may sneak into \nsouthern Mohave County on Thursday afternoon as moisture pushes \nthrough central Arizona. The trough will also support gusty \nsoutherly to southwesterly winds each afternoon, the strongest of \nwhich will peak between 30 and 40 mph across San Bernardino, Clark, \nMohave, and southern Nye counties. Expect highs in the 90s to low \n100s in valleys across the Mojave Desert. \n\nAttention turns to a potential moisture surge this weekend caused by \nthe influence of Tropical Storm Marie. Ensemble members are \ngravitating towards two solutions, one which would take the storm \nwest into the Pacific Ocean, and another which would bring the storm \nnorth towards California. Even if the low stays offshore, \nsouthwesterly flow may be able to pull a decent amount of moisture \ninland if the track is favorable. Models show PWATs increasing to \nthe 1.5 to 2.0 inch range along and south of Interstate 15 between \nSaturday and Monday. Precipitation chances will change based on the \npath of the system and high uncertainty remains at this time.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 12Z Forecast Package...\nAs forecasted, winds have remained elevated overnight at 12-18 kts \nwith sporadic gusts 20-25 kts. Expect S-SW winds remain elevated \nthrough the rest of the morning around 10-15 kts...gusts may drop off \nduring the early morning then return after 16z-17z. Higher \nconfidence in winds remaining S-SW through the period with gusts 25-\n30 kts from 17z-sunset. Thinking S-SW winds will likely remain \nelevated after sunset at 10-15 kts, but confidence is lower if gusts \nwill persist into the overnight hours. Temperatures remain below 100 \ndegrees through the forecast period. No cig or vis concerns. \n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 12Z Forecast Package...Daily wind pattern \nexpected at most terminals through the forecast period with the \nexception of winds remaining elevated early this morning and then \nagain after sunset tonight within the CRV and Las Vegas Valley. Wind \ngusts return late morning through around sunset at 20-30 kts. No \noperationally significant cloud cover though the TAF period.\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Meltzer\nAVIATION...Moore\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
